:: Thomas Study Session 1 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 60>>
You arrive at the library a bit earlier than planned and take a seat at a table near the entrance to ensure <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> sees you. You pull out your homework from the last week or two and begin to go through it. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> said he didn’t want to just copy off of you or have you do it, which is pretty commendable, so you want to be sure you know what you are talking about as you try to explain it. <br>
<br>
You are sitting there for a solid 20 minutes before you realize the time. <span style="color:Yellow">Where could <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> be? You didn’t see him as you left the school, but it wouldn’t make sense for him to forget.</span> He had shared a look with you during English Class that you’re sure was him saying <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’ll see you there!”</span> Maybe you misunderstood? He did say Friday, right? You are going over the request in your head when you suddenly hear a familiar sigh <span style="color:LightGreen">and turn to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> walking in with his little brother <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> in tow.</span> 

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "Thomas",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Uniform",
            Eyes: "Tired",
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
  {
        Name: "Ethan",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Everyday",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’m glad you’re still here.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> says walking over. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> missed the bus, and I was going to take him home, but he insisted on coming.”</span> You smile and say it’s fine, greeting the little boy and giving him a wave. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span>, in turn, looks at you for a solid 5 seconds nibbling on his index finger before turning and wandering off towards the colorful and cozy kid’s section. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> takes a second to catch his breath before pulling out his own homework and begins to go over what he needs the most help with. <br>
<br>
The first bit is spent explaining and giving an overview of recent lessons. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> is quick to understand once you explain and just seems to have missed the lessons that originally explained it all. The main thing he struggles with is History, having a lot of trouble remembering the facts and dates of things. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I just don’t understand why it’s important to remember. When am I going to use this? Math, I get. English is at least interesting, but History? Ugghhh…”</span> He groans, obviously having trouble staying awake as you recount old legislation and the founding of the country. It takes a while to get through it all, but thankfully the Math portion of the homework goes by quickly. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">is actually pretty good when it comes to numbers!</span> 

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "Thomas",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Uniform",
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Alright. That’s today’s homework done as well.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> takes a deep breath in relief, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“only the Science stuff left. I got my art homework done on my own.”</span> With a smirk you ask if you could see said art homework, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> refuses. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I don’t have it on me. And even if I did, I’m not about showing off my art to other people.”</span> You scoff in feigned shock, asking if this is how he treats his friend who spends hours on a Friday night helping him with his homework. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Ha, that’s fair.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> actually chuckles at this, a rare sight. He blushes as you point this out. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Shut up. I can laugh, just not going to sit here giggling about every little thing like some people. But you’re right. You’re doing me a solid favor. Tell you what, I’ll give you one free pass. I’ll draw something for you, whatever you want. I’m not the best, but-”</span> He shrugs and actually gives you a genuine smirk, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“least I can do since you’re helping me out.”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">You smile at his gift, accepting it. Now you just have to ponder what you should have him draw for you.</span> <br>
<br>
As you begin to work on the last bit of homework, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> begins to struggle to stay awake. The talk of scientific formulas and processes battling against his already weakening cognitive ability. At one point he lays his head on the table and stares off towards the kids’ area <span style="color:Pink">where <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> sits upside down on a beanbag staring at a picture book that, from your perspective, is right side up.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> sighs, slowly lifting his head back up to continue his work. <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Focus on helping him<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You decide against prodding <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> for personal information. He asked you here to help him as a friend, the best thing you can do for him is focus on helping him get this homework done to remove a burden from his shoulders. So, you concentrate on helping him with anything he seems to be struggling with and watch as time flies by as the two of you complete the pile of homework he has left. <span style="color:LightGreen">You are actually pretty surprised you manage to get it done so smoothly.</span> <br>
        <br>
        Though you worry for a bit that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> may get bored hanging out here while you work, but he seems to be rather enjoying himself. Well, at least you think he is. The boy doesn’t really change his expression, going from one colorful picture book to another and reading them in all sorts of odd positions. <br>
        <<socialChange "Thomas" 3>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Thomas Study Session 2]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Ask him if he’s been sleeping alright<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        Feeling a bit worried for your friend, since he seems more tired than usual, you ask him if he’s been sleeping alright. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Huh?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> says, sitting up, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oh, yeah. About the same, I guess.”</span> He shrugs, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Like I said, long hours recently. Things should cut back soon. Just a lot of demand at the moment and dad is a big of a deadbeat as ever. Plus, the economy is going to hell.”</span> You blink twice at him, not fully understanding his meaning. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Right, you don’t have to worry about that, I guess.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> stretches back in his chair, staring at the roof for a minute. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Stuff costs more every year and pay doesn’t go up. So, I got to work more to make up the difference, you know? Keep the lights on and the water flowing. It is what it is. Now enough stupid questions, help me finish this before I pass out from boredom.”</span> You nod and continue helping him, <span style="color:Yellow">though you can’t help but feel a little sorry for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span>. Must be rough being the provider of him and his brother.</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">You feel a little more appreciative of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> upon realizing this.</span> <br>
        <<socialChange "Thomas" 3>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Thomas Study Session 2]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<requiresTrait "Nurturing" "Comment on how good of a brother he is">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You smile as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> turns his head towards where <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> sits, now reading another colorful picture book while laying on one of the tables with his feet dangling to one side. <span style="color:Pink">His shoes having fallen to the floor and his head was off the other dangling upside down. His top has also fluttered down, revealing his adorable skinny belly. Interestingly enough, he also seems to be starting to slip out of his far too big shorts, nearly half of the little boy’s White Briefs exposed. It is quite a cute and interesting position, but he must find it comfortable.</span> The boy tilts his head oddly and opens his mouth at one point, looking to be silently mouthing out a word. <span style="color:Pink">You can’t help but notice <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> smile slightly at this.</span> 
        
        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Thomas",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Eyes: "Mad",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“What are you smirking at?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> says with a red face upon seeing you staring. You chuckle and just comment on how good of a brother he is. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Wha-!? Sh- shut it! We’re here to do homework, not discuss my personal life!”</span> You roll your eyes and tell him to take the compliment. Plus, it’s true. You’re pretty family-oriented yourself, with your own little brother Noah, so you understand how he feels. It’s normal for a big brother to look after the little one. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> glares at you for a moment before sighing. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“It’s different for us…”</span> He says quietly, pausing for a moment before realizing the awkward silence this created. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Ju- just focus on getting the homework done!”</span> You decide to drop it for now; it is clear <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> isn’t ready to open up about these things just yet. Still, <span style="color:Pink">you feel glad he is comfortable enough with you to bring <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> around.</span> <br>
        <<socialChange "Thomas" 5>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Thomas Study Session 2]]
    <</replace>>
    <</requiresTrait>>
</div>

:: Thomas Study Session 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 120>>
With the homework finished shortly after, the two of you begin chatting about random things. You find that it is pretty hard to have normal kid conversations with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span>, as talking about the latest popular cartoons, movies, or comics is lost on him. Though he seems to enjoy you recounting the tales of some of the latest interesting ones you’ve seen. That is, <span style="color:Yellow">until, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> suddenly notices the clock and springs to his feet with a curse.</span>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Frown",
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "Thomas",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Uniform",
            Mouth: "Frown",
            Eyes: "Tired",
        },
    },
  {
        Name: "Ethan",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Everyday",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Shit! Is it that late already?”</span> He says, before being shooshed by the very mean-looking librarian. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Fuck, completely lost track of time. I need to hurry, have a shift that’s about to start!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> quickly begins to shove his homework and books into his bag as you help grab the few that he accidentally knocks to the floor. He is just zipping up his bag and flinging it over his shoulders when <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> walks over, hearing the commotion. He tilts his head at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> cutely. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Fu-”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> pauses, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I forgot about you. Shoot.”</span> He thinks for a moment, looking to you with an unsure expression, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Sorry about this, but would you mind taking <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> home for me? If I’m late I’ll be in big trouble and I really don’t want him walking home this late by himself. I wouldn’t ask if it wasn’t important.”</span> <br>
<br>
You nod, telling him it’s no trouble. He doesn’t need to worry, you’ll get that boy home and cozy, no problem. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“If you drop him off at the door, he’ll be fine. He’s pretty good at hanging about by himself until I get off.”</span> You say you wouldn’t mind staying with him until <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> gets off, so he’s not alone, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> is completely against the idea. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“If my dad sees you in the house- <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> will be fine. Thanks, but just drop him off.”</span> He walks over and ruffles his brother’s hair before kneeling down, explaining the situation to him and that you’ll be taking him home. He gives you a curious look, glancing from your feet to your face before leaning in and whispering something softly to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span>. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Right.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> smirks and stands up, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“He says he’s fine with that; Guess he likes you.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> looks back to his brother, who is giving you a strange look that you can’t explain, but is a little eerie. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Thanks again, I’ll pay you back for this and the homework. I gotta run! See ya!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> dashes off, not even giving you a chance to say goodbye. You chuckle as he vanishes, running faster than you’ve ever seen him run before.

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "Ethan",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Everyday",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:Pink">You suddenly feel <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> grab your hand and turn to see him next to you nibbling on his middle finger, staring blankly straight ahead.</span> You ask him if he’s ready to go and he looks up at you and tilts his head. You guess that’s a yes. You lead the boy out and into the streets. The sun has already begun to go down and the streetlights are on. You wonder if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> is afraid of the dark, but don’t see any change in his expression as you continue down Main Street, other than him changing the finger he’s nibbling on to his ring finger. <br>
<br>
This is the first time you’ve been alone with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span>. You’ve only really seen him a handful of times and he’s never spoken to you. You wonder why that is. He certainly can speak, since you’ve noticed him whispering to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> before, but outside of that you’ve never heard a word. He looks like he may be a year or two younger than Noah and he must be at school, based on what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> said. You’d guess he’s just shy, but that’s not the vibe you got from him. <span style="color:Yellow">In fact, thinking about it, you’re not sure what vibe you get from him. He just seems… odd?</span> <br>
<br>
<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    You turn the corner into the trailer park and try to remember which one is <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span>’. As if he read your mind, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> points it out and begins to walk over, now dragging you along by the hand. You follow up to the small trailer’s front door, beginning to wonder if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> has a key or if the door was left unlocked. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> lets go of your hand, grabbing the handle to the door and jimmying it around a bit in a strange method that causes the door to pop open. You chuckle, saying that’s a neat trick. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> responds to this by looking at you and tilting his head once more. <br>
    <br>
    You peer into the trailer, though can’t see much as the inside is pitch black. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> steps inside and kicks his shoes into the darkness before turning back to you. The place honestly looks a little spooky and has a strange musty smell. It must be hard being here by himself. You know <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> said not to, but you can’t help but ask the young boy if he wants you to stay with him a little bit, if he’s scared or lonely. You’re sure <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> wouldn’t mind if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> wanted it. <br>
    <br>
    The boy makes a strange noise and shakes his head, or more so his entire body. You ask if he’s sure and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> responds by walking back in front of you, taking a bandage off his arm, and placing it on your hand, patting it twice. You have no idea what that means, and it’s kind of gross, but you nod along since you doubt you’d get a better explanation. <br>
    <br>
    You step down from the entrance and give <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> a wave, saying goodbye and telling him to have a goodnight. The boy stands at the doorway looking at you, now chewing the neck of his shirt. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> is a cute kid, but he is also very strange. You give him one last smile and wave before turning around to leave. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Bye.”</span> You spin around as you hear the quiet voice and see the door shut gently, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ethan</span> having vanished into the dark trailer. <span style="color:Pink">You smile and continue walking away.</span> <br>
    <<set $ActiveQuests.delete("Thomas: Study Session")>>
    <<set $CompletedQuests.push("Thomas: Study Session")>>
    <<for _i to 0; _i lt $QuestLog.length; _i++>>
        <<if $QuestLog[_i].Name == "Thomas: Study Session">>
            <<set $QuestLog.deleteAt(_i)>>
            <<break>>
        <</if>>
    <</for>>
    <<set $Notifications.push({
        Name: "Quest Completed!",
        Icon: "Quests/Thomas",
        Description: "You helped <span style=\"color:DarkTurquoise\">Thomas</span> finish all of his homework and took <span style=\"color:DarkTurquoise\">Ethan</span> home afterwards. You think the boy is starting to warm up to you.",
    })>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|Trailer Park]]
<</linkreplace>>